ature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f407e028cd6c66367c146c3bfa077d3794d18c53bf45949bf739f1b1cbede93e","event_uuid":"08c312fe-23ef-48ff-83d3-325130714c8e","position":{"commit_sha":"3fe039872414c0035fc8259d3e38cf0c20ac769c","position":"1787003271684446001-08c312fe-23ef-48ff-83d3-325130714c8e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1325054f55a0f60034d8d440e98871e270e4967db0c46b82c9cccd4ed0316581","event_uuid":"c84b8f95-f04e-4c84-b709-de807e512346","position":{"commit_sha":"9e4e8d2ded830350ffcad885a8e3960276a8c4c8","position":"1787005183214357001-c84b8f95-f04e-4c84-b709-de807e512346"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"The ADR task miniscule-unschooled-snowmonkey is modeled as a blocking prerequisite, not a child: Rebar parent-first claim would otherwise force this epic through plan review/start before the ADR and implementation graph exist. The blocks edge enforces ADR-first sequencing while keeping this epic open and unclaimed.","timestamp":1786991513013019001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"ADR 0098 has been drafted and pushed as Gerrit change 1840 in WIP. The draft records the approved operation snapshot, provider-native auth/session injection, static carrier, subprocess, restart/redeploy, observability, and op-cert startup decisions. Generator/index/docs/lint checks pass. The numbered Draft Critique is on miniscule-unschooled-snowmonkey and has no unresolved item. The ADR remains a blocking prerequisite; this epic stays open and unclaimed pending explicit HOLD approval and later implementation decomposition.","timestamp":1786991993184513001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Validated against origin/main 349d91bb27, which includes RP-01 commits 08bcb1f9..f0275172 and accepted ADR 0098. In the fresh origin/main worktree, 34 authoritative RP-01 bounded-operation, request-budget/retry-exhaustion, and candidate-tracing tests passed. Epic material now pins LLMRuntime injection to the existing PydanticAIRunner -> per-run ProviderSession -> one-Agent path and preserves RP-01 budget, complete-or-omit history, cache/accounting, exhaustion, artifact, tracing, usage, and failure behavior. The recovered RP-04 AST ownership guard is also explicit: a separate ownership-direction gate beside check_config_reads.py, local+CI wired, red-proofed across alias/environment access forms, exact justified exceptions only, zero legacy exceptions at cutover. Full validation note: .joe-janitor/rp04-origin-main-validation.md.","timestamp":1786994795746060001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decomposition complete against origin/main/ADR 0098: S1 cotton-only-cuckoo (application-wide shadow OperationSnapshot); S2 titanium-chocolatey-kakapo (reconciler read/check); S3 talismanic-profitable-isopod (apply/Git/child env); S4 distended-bipartisan-arkshell (RP-01 ProviderSession auth injection); S5 typical-neutral-waterbug (MCP/review-bot startup bindings); S6 ultrashort-immoderate-seriema (op-cert startup signer); S7 junior-lepidolite-boa (AST ownership gate, generated docs, canaries, legacy removal). Graph: S2->S1; S3->S2; S4->S1; S5->S4; S6->S1; S7->{S3,S5,S6}. Each child has binary behavioral ACs, RED->GREEN tiers/oracles, exact file impact, and expand/contract rollback. S1/S2/S4 use subsystem-local modules so S2, S4, and S6 can proceed conflict-free after S1. Blocked descendants will not be force-reviewed; they re-enter review when dependencies close.","timestamp":1786995540529726001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final origin/main/decomposition verification: origin/main remains 349d91bb27 with landed RP-01 08bcb1f9..f0275172; the recorded 34-test RP-01 authoritative oracle is still the S4 baseline. S7 now makes the centralized-config guard resistant to ordinary future bypasses by deriving config/credential names from authoritative registries, failing unowned new names, resolving direct/import/local aliases and attribute/subscript/literal-getattr environment access, requiring exact path+symbol+rationale exceptions, running via make lint and CI parity, and reaching zero legacy exceptions at cutover. It remains a deterministic change detector supplemented by S1-S6 behavioral oracles, not a security-sandbox claim. S1 cotton-only-cuckoo is certified PASS at 349d91bb27 after pinning explicit operation input to resolve_with_sources(cli_overrides=...) with existing cli provenance, canonical serialization/hashing reuse, the default-enabled REBAR_OPERATION_SNAPSHOT_SHADOW rollback switch, and fail-open isolation for non-config shadow defects. Descendants remain unreviewed until their dependencies close; no force review was used. Recovery note: .joe-janitor/rp04-origin-main-validation.md.","timestamp":1786997078189775001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[AC10 canary — RP-04 S1] Gerrit change 1841 (S1 a377) pushed 2026-08-17T22:19:43Z. Commit c006f54. Auth-source kind for the review-bot/CI run: Gerrit HTTP credential (git credential helper) + GitHub Actions default. Gates in flight: LLM-Review (AWS review bot on new code), Verified (GitHub Actions CI reconciler on new code). Local preflight green: make lint (complexity new=0), make typecheck (556 files), held-out oracle 32/32. Retry count: 0. No credential/path/secret leakage in shadow diagnostics (verified by held-out redaction oracle).","timestamp":1787005183214357001}],"created_at":1786990959694662001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"581e577d-6432-4a12-8439-6483294756f1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2704-39ae-16f5-4e96"},{"link_uuid":"bdfb4151-b9e5-4b51-8aea-7fbfa94f343e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9b75-8bb5-601d-402d"},{"link_uuid":"361dc710-a838-41ff-b94b-7a46b79be79a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"77c0-9fe4-e0eb-4073"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nRebar resolves configuration through multiple authorities during one operation, and some backends reread ambient state after receiving explicit config. Authentication is also composed inconsistently across LLM, Git, bridge, MCP, review-bot, observability, and op-cert boundaries. This can change behavior mid-operation, discard an explicit choice, expose static credentials to unrelated children, or fall back through an unintended identity. RP-04 establishes one application-wide composition contract without making Rebar a credential store.\n\nThe approved research is on `relevant-liberal-xantus`; ADR 0098 is authoritative. Landed RP-01 (`08bcb1f9`–`f0275172`) is the LLM baseline RP-04 must extend.\n\n## Approved design\n- Resolve one immutable, serializable, non-secret `OperationSnapshot` at each operation boundary. Precedence is explicit operation input > environment > project config > user config > schema default.\n- Resolve repository root separately: explicit `repo_root` > `REBAR_ROOT` > Git top-level/current directory. Interpret winning relative paths against that root.\n- CLI composes once per invocation; MCP and Python once per operation; long-running processes also own startup deployment policy and live runtime bindings. An in-progress operation does not reread environment, files, cwd, or global config.\n- Compose subsystem-local `GitRuntime`, `LLMRuntime`, and selected `BridgeRuntime` bindings. SDKs/helpers own credential issuance, storage, refresh, expiry, invalidation, and native precedence; Rebar-owned factories retain transport/output policy. `LLMRuntime` enters only RP-01's existing `PydanticAIRunner` -> per-run `ProviderSession` -> one-Agent path. Preserve its budget, complete-or-omit retry history, cache/accounting, typed exhaustion, artifacts, tracing, usage, and failure translation. No arbitrary client/runner injection or second scheduler/owner/path.\n- Represent unavoidable static material with provider-specific, non-serializable Pydantic `SecretStr`/`SecretBytes` carriers, revealing it only in the sending adapter. Do not add a universal secret broker, central credential union, automatic keyring fallback, or application-owned cloud-secret retrieval.\n- Trusted same-capability children inherit ambient environment for Git/SSH/AWS/proxy/CA compatibility. Rebar never installs credentials through global `os.environ` mutation. An owning child receives its adapter overlay; unrelated sibling children remove exact secret names declared by other Rebar adapters. Deployment/container/process boundaries remain the primary isolation mechanism.\n- Static bindings rotate on restart/redeploy; SDK-native refresh remains SDK-owned.\n- Op-cert accepts exactly one of `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` (preferred) or `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY`, validates before queue/worker/network/workspace creation, and copies the key into a process-owned 0700 directory/0600 file. Jobs receive context-local signer/principal/push-policy bindings. Remove runtime SSM/boto3/region coupling and per-job retrieval. Deployment may retain ADR 0049's SSM-at-rest source by injecting/mounting the resolved secret before process startup.\n- Fail closed when explicit provider/profile/project/auth composition fails; never retry anonymously or as another ambient principal. Preserve optional write-only Langfuse/OTLP observability's fail-open/no-op behavior.\n- Add a portable-local-and-CI AST ownership gate beside `check_config_reads.py`. It derives config/credential names from authoritative registries, rejects reads/reloads/defaults below approved seams, red-proves aliases/access shapes, permits only exact path/symbol+rationale exceptions, and reaches zero legacy exceptions at cutover.\n\n## Scope\nRP-04 only: central non-secret resolution/provenance, operation projections, runtime bindings, provider-native auth injection, static-secret handling, op-cert startup composition, all affected CLI/library/MCP/reconciler/hosted consumers, ownership gates, generated operator documentation, migration, and canaries. RP-02/RP-03 and RP-05/RP-06 remain separate.\n\nExplicit corrections: CLI input outranks environment for `tracker.dir`; malformed config fails before effects; backends stop reloading; supplied Python config stays authoritative; defaults move to the schema; tracker layout reaches every owner; Jira Cloud write scope loses `DIG`. Other auth, redaction, retry, TLS, and output behavior changes require an explicit child decision and test.\n\n## Migration / rollback\nExpand in shadow mode, prove parity/deltas and non-leakage, cut consumers over behind compatibility facades, add gates/docs/canaries, then remove legacy paths. Before write cutover, disable shadow composition to roll back; afterward require the snapshot-aware compatibility floor. Stored ticket/bridge formats do not change, and parity diagnostics never persist credentials.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CLI, MCP, Python, and direct reconciler paths produce equivalent non-secret behavior from the approved precedence/root contract; a captured operation is stable across environment/file/cwd mutation while the next operation observes the change.\n- [ ] Every affected consumer receives an immutable projection/runtime binding and no in-progress operation rereads ambient state.\n- [ ] A portable-local-and-CI AST ownership gate derives names from authoritative registries and rejects direct/aliased `load_config`, ambient config/credential reads, backend reloads, and configurable adapter defaults below approved seams; exact path/symbol+rationale exceptions contain no post-cutover legacy entry.\n- [ ] The LLM cutover injects provider-native auth/session capability only through the landed RP-01 `ProviderSession` builders; RP-01's one-run/one-Agent request budget, complete-or-omit retry history, cache/accounting, typed exhaustion, final artifacts, candidate tracing, usage, and failure behavior remain green in authoritative offline oracles and bounded live Anthropic/Bedrock cache/auth canaries.\n- [ ] Git and bridge factories preserve provider-native auth lifecycles and instantiate only the selected integration; missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth fails before network/write without anonymous, cross-provider, or alternate-principal fallback.\n- [ ] Secret canaries are absent from repr, equality/hash, serialization, snapshots, fingerprints, caches, provenance, exceptions, logs, output, argv, URL/query strings, subprocess siblings, and CLI/MCP schemas, verified at behavioral boundaries.\n- [ ] Same-capability children preserve unknown ambient/native-chain variables, owning children receive only their overlay, unrelated siblings lose exact Rebar-declared secret names, and concurrent operations observe no global environment mutation.\n- [ ] Op-cert enforces its exclusive startup sources, fails invalid composition before service work, uses a stable process-owned 0700/0600 copy and context-local signer, observes replacement only after restart, deletes only its copy, and has no application runtime SSM/boto3/region dependency.\n- [ ] Generated config/security/operator docs cover precedence, lifecycles, restart/redeploy rotation, provider ownership, observability's exception, subprocess limitations, and deliberate behavior deltas; drift checks detect schema/docs divergence.\n- [ ] Legacy ambient/per-job composition is removed only after focused suites and bounded live paths pass; rollback retains accurate non-secret diagnostics.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] AWS review-bot and reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live canaries pass after cutover without credential leakage or unauthorized fallback. Epic comments record run/change IDs, timestamps, selected provider/auth-source kind, retry counts, and redacted outcomes.\n\n## Sequencing\nADR 0098 is merged. Create and link vertical implementation children with behavioral oracles and exact file impact before reviewing or claiming this epic.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/","reason":"Application-wide operation snapshot, config composition, provider runtime bindings, adapter factories, subprocess environments, and op-cert startup composition."},{"path":"tests/","reason":"Cross-surface precedence, auth lifecycle, leakage, subprocess, concurrency, op-cert, migration, and regression coverage."},{"path":"docs/","reason":"ADR, architecture/config/security/operator guidance, generated documentation, and migration/rollback documentation."},{"path":"infra/","reason":"Hosted review-bot/op-cert deployment injection, runtime file ownership, and bounded-live canaries."},{"path":"scripts/","reason":"Structural ownership and schema/documentation drift checks."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","77c0-9fe4-e0eb-4073"],["relates_to","9b75-8bb5-601d-402d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"11b86e42-71f8-474f-94bf-da2a87dc5eed","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","rp04","architecture","config","secrets","security"],"ticket_id":"e215-ab23-ed6a-4791","ticket_type":"epic","title":"RP-04 — Operation-scoped configuration and provider-auth composition","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["75043ed6-6a66-4b50-8942-ecfcd45a8cf3","2ed93b6d-69aa-42a2-9a29-5bf60749bbc2","9c9b98c4-437b-4dce-9e64-fddbbd84ae53","78ed8d0d-e373-4d77-8fb1-da7527a22aa6","fc40e990-d3d8-4fe7-a3c8-c6bd554f8536","f1f21ea8-3178-44cd-8e4d-39e755f3c43a","bdfb4151-b9e5-4b51-8aea-7fbfa94f343e","361dc710-a838-41ff-b94b-7a46b79be79a","0a034ca0-60e4-4092-ba0e-e0164d6a9abc","11b86e42-71f8-474f-94bf-da2a87dc5eed","08c312fe-23ef-48ff-83d3-325130714c8e","c84b8f95-f04e-4c84-b709-de807e512346"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787011552048711899,"uuid":"61f555fb-1138-48db-bbeb-40e317956bce"}